# What must never enter a published image.
#
# `.env` first and by name: this image is published to a public registry, and a secret
# that reaches it is a secret that cannot be recalled. The build never needs one - every
# value is supplied at run time - so nothing here is a trade-off.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not secrets, but not the application either. Tests, docs and fixtures would enlarge the
# image and its scan surface without a single one of them ever executing.
test
docs
coverage
*.spec.ts
*.e2e-spec.ts

# Rebuilt inside the image. Copying either from the host would ship whatever the host
# happened to have, including a `dist/` compiled from uncommitted source.
node_modules
dist

# Repository furniture.
.git
.github
.harness
.agents
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
